+## Governed Bulk Intent, Custody And Recovery
+
+Use `BulkOperationClientService` and `BulkOperationStateService.createSession()`
+with its `BulkOperationSession`. Core owns transport, validation and technical
+custody; Table and CRUD consume that same path. Inspect installed/public source
+before adopting it; do not retain a second client or the previous sync-only state
+service as a compatibility lane. Do not create host-local operation bindings when
+metadata already publishes them.
+
+Consume only the modes declared by the current descriptor and supported by the
+client: `SYNC` or `ASYNC`, `EXPLICIT`, `PER_ITEM`, with `DOMAIN_COMMAND`,
+`UNIFORM_UPDATE` or `PER_ITEM_UPDATE` as declared. Enum members alone do not prove
+QUERY or ATOMIC support. Preserve operation/group/method/path, resource, origin,
+request/response schema bindings and exact wire IDs. Read each selected resource's
+original strong ETag through its canonical self GET and declared identity accessor;
+reject weak, missing or cross-identity versions. A schema ETag is not a resource
+version. SET and CLEAR come from published writable/clearable fields; CLEAR omits
+value rather than sending null as an invented clear convention.
+
+Evaluate one immutable intent without domain effects, display its protected preview,
+and require a separate explicit confirmation of a READY proposal. The session owns
+one proposal and its Idempotency-Key. Before any confirmation POST, persist and
+read back the technical custody record; storage failure blocks dispatch. Confirmation
+sends the retained proposalId and the same key, not a replacement evaluation or the
+original target payload. Fingerprint the contract and resolved addresses; changed
+metadata/origin blocks recovery rather than silently moving the intent.
+
+After a lost response/503, remount or reload, recover fresh discovery and protected
+proposal/execution reads first. Recovery never confirms automatically. An explicit
+retry for the same intent reuses the original key. Retain only technical references,
+execution mode and contract fingerprint in session storage; never persist READY,
+permissions, grants, preview/results or business payload as authority. An existing or
+malformed unfinished record must not be overwritten by another session. Custody is
+bounded to that browser session; do not claim durable cross-device recovery.
+
+Treat HTTP 202 as an accepted response, not a status enum. QUEUED, RUNNING and
+CANCEL_REQUESTED are ongoing execution states. Read authoritative status,
+page results and offer cooperative cancellation only through the declared binding.
+Distinguish COMPLETED from partial errors, CANCELLED, STOPPED and
+RECONCILIATION_REQUIRED. The latter or unknown/indeterminate totals do not authorize
+custody cleanup or a success message. `complete()` is an explicit cleanup after a
+fresh authorized resolved terminal result, never after a transport failure, closed
+dialog or uncertain execution.
+
+Separate custody from permission to display retained data. On protected
+401/403/404/410 or context/scope loss, invalidate projections immediately while
+retaining an already dispatched intent. Use authorization epochs so late successes
+or result pages cannot restore data. Before redisplay, require current authorized
+reads for the retained resource/operation and the server-approved scope. Where an
+enterprise integration is configured or was confirmed, honor its ready identity,
+organization/profile/version and ACL invalidation fences. A provided-in-root context
+service alone does not make a standalone host require corporate context. Preserve
+history across host remounts; loss after confirmation cannot silently downgrade to
+standalone. Without that integration, cookie/session authentication and fresh backend
+operation grants still govern execution; do not fabricate READY, actor or tenant.
+
+Do not equate protected read authorization with creator continuity or confirmation
+permission. SDK readers delegate full-target authorization to the host provider; the
+Quickstart participant provider can permit another currently authorized requester to
+read. That is lawful delegated read, not a way to change the retained intent's creator.
+Confirmation/idempotency is still bound to the authenticated subject and original
+intent scope at the server. Keep technical custody if identity is unknown; fresh
